  	This vesion of poker was written under early BSD 4.2 (DYNIX),    with a UCB universe.	It is not guaranteed to work when compiled in the att universe     (System V release 2) due to differences in curses.	The file poker.h should be edited to define how the instructions    are to be displayed. /usr/ucb/more is used, but this can be altered,    and so must the path to the file poker_rules.		The title screen (with the implementors address) is displayed    by the procedure title(), which is in p_scr.c	Most bugs have been removed, any that exist are in the hand    recognition routines, and do not appear often. Anything that looks     suspicious is probably just a design feature that you do not agree     with, or is due to the compiler and universe used.	I make this statement because I will soon loose my account, and    will not be able to help with queries. The code is however, fairly    well structured, so it should not be too hard to modify.